<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Proton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1983–</span> · Also known as Proton Holdings</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Proton is Malaysia's national car company, founded in 1983 on the initiative of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahathir-mohamad">Mahathir Mohamad</a> in partnership with Mitsubishi. Its first model, the Proton Saga, went into production in 1985 and dominated the domestic market behind <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protective-tariff">protective tariffs</a>. Part of the government's heavy-industry drive, the company sold a large minority stake to the Chinese carmaker Geely in 2017.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/proton.jpg" alt="Proton" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arpad Horvath · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Quark_structure_proton.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
